# Managed by the open-forti-manager package — do not edit.
#
# Lets the native Fortinet SSL-VPN client configure its VPN routes and
# per-link DNS without a password prompt on connect. The grant is a single
# helper binary, callable with NO arguments: it reads a typed JSON request on
# stdin and performs only validated operations —
#   * on the caller's own VPN TUN device (vpn*, owned by the calling user,
#     matching interface index), or
#   * gateway host routes (/32) that only replicate the current physical path,
#     and deletion of routes the app itself created (route marker proto 186).
# It cannot take other interfaces down, flush them, change their DNS, or run
# arbitrary programs. It does NOT grant a passwordless root shell.
#
# Applies to members of the 'sudo' group (Ubuntu/Debian administrators), who can
# already run these operations with a password — this only removes the prompt.
%sudo ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/open-forti-manager-net ""
